#
# Commit-msg hook: the sign-off every commit carries, and the hygiene
# rules for agent-authored commits.
#
# Runs three Python checks in order; any one's failure rejects:
#   0. tools/check-dco.py
#      Rejects a commit with no `Signed-off-by:` line (`git commit -s`).
#      Applies to every commit, by a person or an agent: the line
#      certifies the Developer Certificate of Origin (CONTRIBUTING.md).
#   1. tools/check-claude-staged-files.py (H1, 2026-04-23)
#      Rejects commits that bear a "Co-Authored-By:" trailer naming an
#      agent (tools/_agent.py) without a matching "Staged files:"
#      section. Catches file-list sweeps where the body drifted from
#      `git diff --cached`.
#   2. tools/check-preflight-discipline.py (sticky preflight, 2026-04-25)
#      Rejects commits that stage a file which was already dirty at the
#      start of the current Claude session AND was never preflighted
#      by this session. Catches within-file sweeps that H1 misses
#      because H1 only checks file-list correspondence, not per-hunk
#      authorship — the 6th-recurrence shape (commit 4d4a4ab).
#
# A person's manual commits (no agent trailer) pass through checks 1
# and 2 untouched. Check 2 reads Claude Code's session state and stays
# Claude-only. Sticky-preflight gate is also bypassed when
# CLAUDE_PREFLIGHT_SESSION is unset (gradual rollout).
#
# Bypass: `git commit --no-verify` (discouraged).

set -e

cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"

python3 tools/check-dco.py "$1"
python3 tools/check-claude-staged-files.py "$1"
python3 tools/check-preflight-discipline.py "$1"
